this is the culmination really of a  six-week battle between  peloton interactive the company that uh  floated on the stock market a year or so  ago and has  achieved cult status really with a lot  of investors and followers  and the consumer product safety  commission which is the main  watchdog in the united states  responsible for overseeing  businesses that sell items to the public  now what happened on  the 18th of march was that pelleted  admitted as you say that a child had  been killed  following an accident with one of the  treadmills but they refused to  instigate a product recall they also  quibbled very very publicly with  the regulator the uh cpsc about the  number of incidents that had been  involved the cpsc made clear that they  thought there have been around 70  incidents or injuries involving the treb  plus and uh  right throughout this whole saga peliton  have said that was misleading and  inaccurate and they were playing down  the number of uh incidents that have  been involved in an attempt to see off a  recall well today they've caved in and  said that there will have to be  a recall so the product can't be sold to  the public anymore now interestingly  this isn't this is not a cheap item  it retails in the united states for  around 4295 dollars  hundred around three pounds in this  country it was sold as you were saying  earlier by  invitation only to uh members of peloton  it has some 3.1 million members right  around the world  and uh so it's really not very clear  just how many people  have bought this piece of kit as i say  it is not a cheap piece of  equipment and it's also not known how  many of them are on sale in this country  either bear in mind this is an american  product recall since then the company  has been besieged by  lawyers trying to instigate class  actions because it's had an impact  on the share price and i can tell you  right now peloton shares are down by  some six  and a half percent following this news  which as i say represents something  of a capitulation to uh the america to  the regulator responsible here  now interestingly if you dig around  there are quite a lot of accidents that  involve treadmills not just the uh tread  plus as i say this is a particular  incident that involved one child  of whom little is known by the way other  than a report that was in the new york  post  a short while ago which said that the  child involved the injuries were  very unusual that was the highly unusual  that was the terminology that this  source  to the new york post used but i can tell  you uh  the uh statistics on the treadmill  injuries in 2018-19 alone  in the united states there were some 17  deaths as a result  of treadmills not the peloton treb plus  here but  all treadmills and during that period 22  and a half  thousand americans had to visit accident  and emergency  as a result of uh misuse of a treadmill  so  it's a it's a grown-up piece of kit  needs to be taken seriously but as i say  this is a major capitulation on the part  of peloton  interactive the statement from the chief  executive john foley  says the decision to recall both  products was the right thing to do for  peloton's members and their families  i want to be clear peloton made a  mistake in our initial response  to the consumer product safety  commission's request that we  recall the tread plus we should have  engaged more productively with them from  the outset  and for that i apologize today's  announcement reflects the recognition  that by working closely with the cpsc we  can increase safety awareness  for our members so a major climb down  from peloton the shares are falling as i  say by some six and a half percent and  that statement really does look like a  bit of an attempt belatedly to cover the  company's backside with the regulator
 

